    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d4">

                <pb facs="0084" n="918" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v02/pg918"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9135</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-18">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 18, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to your letter of June 4, 1918,
                    enclosing a copy of a note from the British Ambassador in which he announces
                    that his Government proposes, on the advice of the War Trade Advisory Committee,
                    to make certain additions to the list of British absolute contraband, and
                    inquiring whether this Government would be prepared <pb facs="0085" n="919"
                        xml:id="pg919"/> to concur in these proposed modifications, I have the honor
                    to forward herewith a copy of an opinion by the Judge Advocate General of this
                    Department on the subject, which opinion has the approval of the Department.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Josephus Daniels</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d4-a1.xml" xpointer="d4-a1"/>
            </div>
